cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this database or its analysis, please cite it as below, and cite the original data depositors listed in MANIFEST.tsv."
title: "AstroRegolith: an open database and growth-anchored reanalysis of plant growth in lunar, Martian and asteroid regolith"
abstract: >-
  An open, server-free database for plant growth in regolith. It catalogues the
  regolith-relevant holdings of NASA's Open Science Data Repository (nine
  biological studies) and Physical Sciences Informatics system (six curated
  investigations), characterises candidate substrates against returned lunar
  soil, and re-analyses NASA OSD-476 — Arabidopsis thaliana grown in Apollo 11,
  12 and 17 regolith — by joining each RNA-seq sample to the growth trajectory of
  the individual plant it came from. That linkage, possible because the deposit
  recorded a plate and a twelve-timepoint leaf count against each sequenced
  plant, identifies 299 genes whose expression tracks measured growth in both a
  full and an Apollo-only analysis, 82 of which are not detected by the published
  substrate contrasts. Includes the harvest and analysis code, harmonised
  phenotype and expression tables, a static web database with in-browser
  calibration-marker analysis, an Epicollect5 contribution workflow, and a
  manuscript.
type: software
